---
import AsterLayout from "../../layouts/AsterLayout.astro";
import { ASTER_DEX_ID, AUTHORS, PERSON_ID, SITE_URL } from "../../entity";
import { buildAsterPageGraph, buildBreadcrumbs } from "../../lib/schema";
import { ASTER_BRIDGE_FACTS, ASTER_DOCS, ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED } from "../../data/aster";

const url = `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/aster-chain/`;
const description =
  "Aster Chain explained: PoSA consensus, 50 ms blocks, 100k TPS, zero gas, the 14-exchange oracle, cross/isolated margin and the 3-of-4 bridge.";

const articleNode = {
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "@id": `${url}#article`,
  headline: "Aster Chain",
  alternativeHeadline: "Aster Chain: the settlement layer behind Aster DEX",
  name: "Aster Chain: the settlement layer behind Aster DEX",
  description,
  url,
  mainEntityOfPage: url,
  inLanguage: "en",
  datePublished: "2026-11-24",
  dateModified: ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED,
  author: { "@id": AUTHORS.kirsty.id },
  editor: { "@id": AUTHORS.maksim.id },
  publisher: { "@id": PERSON_ID },
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/#collection` },
  articleSection: "Infrastructure",
  about: [
    { "@id": ASTER_DEX_ID },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Blockchain", sameAs: "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q20514253" },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Proof of authority" },
  ],
  citation: [
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Aster Chain overview", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}aster-chain/overview` },
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "What is Aster?", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}overview/what-is-aster` },
  ],
};

const breadcrumbs = buildBreadcrumbs(`${url}#breadcrumbs`, [
  { name: "Home", url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
  { name: "Aster DEX", url: `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/` },
  { name: "Aster Chain", url },
]);

const graph = buildAsterPageGraph([articleNode, breadcrumbs]);
---

<AsterLayout
  title="Aster Chain — PoSA, 50 ms Blocks and the 14-Exchange Oracle | Maksim Sokal"
  description={description}
  canonical={url}
  graph={graph}
  trail={[{ label: "Aster Chain" }]}
  modified={new Date(ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED)}
>
  <header class="space-y-5 max-w-3xl">
    <span class="text-xs font-mono text-sky-400 uppercase tracking-widest block">Infrastructure</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-medium text-3xl md:text-4xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight leading-tight">
      Aster Chain
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Aster is not a contract deployed on someone else's chain. Trading settles on Aster Chain, a purpose-built Layer 1
      with its own consensus, oracle and clearinghouse. That design explains the fee structure, the privacy model and
      several of the risks.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400">
      Verified <time datetime={ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}>{ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}</time> ·{" "}
      <a href={`${ASTER_DOCS}aster-chain/overview`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">official overview</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3" aria-label="Chain specifications">
    <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-4">
      <span class="block text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-400">Block time</span>
      <span class="text-lg font-display text-slate-100">50 ms</span>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-4">
      <span class="block text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-400">Throughput</span>
      <span class="text-lg font-display text-slate-100">100k TPS</span>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-4">
      <span class="block text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-400">Gas</span>
      <span class="text-lg font-display text-slate-100">0</span>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-4">
      <span class="block text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-400">Consensus</span>
      <span class="text-lg font-display text-slate-100">PoSA</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="consensus-heading">
    <h2 id="consensus-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">PoSA: performance with a validator assumption</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Proof-of-Staked Authority combines staking incentives with a reputation-based validator set. It is the reason the
      chain can produce 50 ms blocks without a public mempool auction. The trade-off is the same as every PoA-derived
      design: you are trusting a defined validator set more than you would trust a fully permissionless one.
    </p>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      During Phase 1, external validator participation is not supported. Observer nodes and staking validators are
      described as future work. Until then, decentralisation is a roadmap item, not a current property.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="oracle-heading">
    <h2 id="oracle-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Oracle and clearinghouse</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">14-source weighted median</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Each validator calculates a weighted median spot price from 14 major exchanges. The oracle feeds funding, mark
          price, TP/SL triggers and liquidation. A median across venues is harder to manipulate than a single feed, but
          it is still an input assumption.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">Clearinghouse and margin</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          The clearinghouse tracks margin balances and positions. Deposits enter cross margin by default; traders can
          switch a position to isolated margin. Each perpetual market has an independent order book.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="bridge-heading">
    <h2 id="bridge-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">The bridge is the trust boundary</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Trading is on Aster Chain, but deposits come from five chains. The bridge is where most users first interact with
      validator assumptions.
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
      {ASTER_BRIDGE_FACTS.map((fact) => (
        <li>{fact}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      The five bridge addresses are maintained in the <a href="/aster-dex/contracts/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">contract registry</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="open-heading">
    <h2 id="open-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">What is open source — and what is not</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Bridge contracts and related code are published on the Smart Contracts page. The docs state that core chain
      contracts and RPC infrastructure are not open-sourced at this time, to protect the matching engine and during early
      deployment. That is a material limitation for independent verification: the parts that decide execution are not
      available for review.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-6 space-y-2">
    <h2 class="font-display font-medium text-sm text-slate-200 tracking-wide">How to weigh it</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      Aster Chain is a performance-first design with a credible privacy model and a defined validator set. It is not a
      trustless chain in the same sense as Ethereum. If your threat model includes validator collusion or closed-source
      execution, size positions accordingly. If you mainly care about privacy from public observers and CEX-like speed,
      the architecture is coherent.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Related: <a href="/aster-dex/privacy/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">privacy mechanics</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/deposits-withdrawals/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">deposits and withdrawals</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-[#1e293b]/60 pt-6">
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Written by <a href="/kirsty-moreland/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Kirsty Moreland</a> · Technical review by{" "}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Maksim Sokal</a> ·
      <a href="/disclosure/" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-sky-300">Disclosure</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</AsterLayout>
